# Entry selects the existing data description before its source field is replaced.
# The first read computes that description once; the next call selects the new source value.
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: the structural link carries the scene -- the record Code is written inside Inputs next to the
# computed description `int: x tick()`; main selects it by the alias `@: body Inputs\Code` and calls
# `call(code := body)` twice (the translation of the machine row frame_description_gc). The first launch reads the
# description once (ticks 1, total 80); the body writes `data\x := 9` into the parent, so the second launch reads the
# new source (total 18) and the root read gives 9. The former records `call(source; body)` still have the two
# positionals of [args, code]; the substitution of DATA is removed, and they answer 5 on this scene.
# Norm: the book #structural-call, #call-frame-20261115 (the read of a computed place executes the declaration's
# expression once at the read).
Observed:
    int: ticks 0
    int: first 0
    int: second 0
    int: source 0
end: Observed
fn: tick () int
    Observed\ticks := Observed\ticks + 1
    return: 40
Inputs:
    int: x tick()
    @: observed Observed
    Code:
        data\x := 9
        int: total x + x
        if: observed\first = 0
            observed\first := total
        else:
            observed\second := total
    end: Code
end: Inputs
Main:
    @: body Inputs\Code
    call(code := body)
    call(code := body)
    Observed\source := Inputs\x
